text:
alex_cheng: RFC draft up for review — SDK streaming + retries ergonomics. Link: https://docs.redwood.ai/rfcs/sdk-stream-retries-v0.1. I want to lock scope for launch: retry/backoff defaults, hedging API, and streaming reconnect/handshake behavior. PTAL :eyes:

maria_gomez: skimmed. overall looks good 👍. Quick Q: do we define explicit SLOs for streaming reconnects vs request-level retries? We should capture failure modes (truncated streams, half-open, dup chunks).

benji_kaplan: +1 on failure modes. Implementation note: avoid automatic message reordering. Suggest: default autoReconnect=false; provide optional autoReconnect:{mode:'resume'|'restart', maxAttempts:3}. Resume needs server support (resume_token).

sophie_ng: acceptance criteria proposals: 1) client exposes explicit retry/backoff config and default is conservative (exp backoff, maxAttempts=4). 2) streaming has opt-in autoReconnect with resume token. 3) client emits telemetry for reconnects, dupes, dropped events. 4) docs include migration notes.

alex_cheng: proposed API example for ergonomics — please comment: ```js
const client = new Redwood({
  retry: { mode: 'exponential', baseMs: 200, maxAttempts: 4 },
  streaming: { autoReconnect: false, resumeWindowMs: 30000 }
});
const stream = client.chat.stream({ model: 'redwood-2b' });
stream.on('data', (msg) => console.log(msg));
// to enable hedging for short requests
client.defaults.hedging = { enabled: false }
```

ciara-bot: RFC draft published to staging docs: https://staging.docs.redwood.ai/rfcs/sdk-stream-retries-v0.1 ; review deadline Fri 2026-03-26 17:00 UTC.

benji_kaplan: edge-case: server might resend overlapping chunks after reconnect. Client should de-dupe using sequence_id if present. If no sequence_id, fall back to checksum-based dedupe within a small sliding window. Also handle partial utf-8 chunk boundaries.

maria_gomez: launch gating metrics suggestion: median reconnect latency <200ms on local infra, no memory leak under sustained 5k streams, and end-to-end ordering must be preserved for ordered streams in 99.9% of reconnects. Also need a small compatibility test matrix for older language SDKs.

alex_cheng: noted. Question to the group: hedging default on or off? My leaning is off — hedging changes billing and non-idempotent semantics.

sophie_ng: hedging should be opt-in. Support teams asked for a graceful shutdown hook so apps can drain pending tokens/events before process exit. Add to acceptance criteria.

alex_cheng: ok I'll update the PRD to include the acceptance criteria, test harness sketch, and the scope (defaults: conservative retries, hedging off, streaming autoReconnect opt-in with resume). Will also add example migration notes and a sample harness for dup/ordering tests. Plan to push updates by EOD. Thanks all :pray:
